  "solution": {
    "text": "The equation of the tangent at <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3,2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> to the parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<br /><math><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />or <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Since the tangent at one end of the focal chord is parallel to the normal at the other end, the slope of the normal at the other end of the focal chord is <math><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  }
